  "doc.title": "What the Yield Curve Says · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "Line up one borrower's one-, two- … ten-year interest rates and you get a curve the news calls “inverted”, “steepening” or “a recession signal”. Starting from zero-coupon bonds, this essay separates forward rates, expectations and the term premium, then covers duration, convexity, the three ways a curve moves and why it inverts, and moves on to corporate bonds: default probability, recovery, credit spreads and why junk-bond defaults cluster, ending with what the curve actually did in 2022–2026. Twelve hands-on models; mechanisms only, not investment advice.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
